PICT-Python
Copyright 2026 Daniel Chan

This is an INDEPENDENT EDUCATIONAL REIMPLEMENTATION in pure Python and NumPy of the numerical
methods described by PICT, the differentiable GPU multi-block PISO solver from the Physics-based
Simulation group at the Technical University of Munich:

    https://github.com/tum-pbs/PICT
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

It is NOT a fork of that project and contains none of its source code. Where this port follows
PICT's design -- the conservative Thomas & Lombard metrics, the multi-block connection model, the
PISO corrector structure -- it was reimplemented from the described method rather than
translated, and the differences are documented in reference/.

